	(text_box "Auto reset circuit\nAllows PC to put ESP32 into programming mode over USB\n2 NPN + 2 10k base resistors\n\nNPN\nMFG: S8050 J3Y(RANGE:200-350)\nLCSC: C2146\n\n\nSchematic Order (Common Circuit):\nTransistor 1 (Q1): Base connected to DTR (via 10k resistor), Collector to GPIO0, Emitter to Q2 Collector.\nTransistor 2 (Q2): Base connected to RTS (via 10k resistor), Collector to Q1 Emitter, Emitter to GND. Actually, the more typical circuit uses the \"cross-coupled\" NPN configuration:\nQ1 Base connected to DTR (via 10k), Collector to EN, Emitter to GND.\nQ2 Base connected to RTS (via 10k), Collector to GPIO0, Emitter to GND.\n(And the cross-logic to prevent both from being low at the same time: EN is pulled low only if DTR is high and RTS is low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
